---
title: Vegan Chocolate Truffle Torte
source_url: https://www.gordonramsayrestaurants.com/recipes/vegan-chocolate-truffle-torte
Author: Gordon Ramsay
---

Mix all the ingredients for the base together in a bowl: @cocoa nib{38%g}, @pistachios{38%g}(roasted & chopped), @vegan digestive biscuits{38%g}(crushed), @vegan chocolate{38%g}(70% melted), and @salt{pinch}

Press the mix firmly into the base of a #20cm shallow flan ring{}.

Set the base in the fridge for ~{15%minutes} before filling with the truffle tofu mixture.

Gently melt the @vegan chocolate{150%g}(70%) in a bowl, over hot water. Stir until completely smooth and melted.

Blitz the @silken tofu{150%g} in a liquidiser until smooth. Add the melted chocolate and @strong coffee{25%ml}(1 Double Espresso) to the tofu in the liquidiser and continue to blend until well mixed and completely smooth.

Pour the chocolate tofu into the tin, over the biscuit base & smooth the top.

Chill in the fridge until firm for approximately ~{4%hours}.

Place a slice of the torte on a plate and serve with a few segments of @oranges{4}(segmented) and a sprinkling of @pistachios{100%g}(roasted & chopped).

> You can subtitute the coffee for a liqueur, e.g. amaretto, for a richer taste.
